Delta since v14 touching WS-D: the design's Status paragraph lists what v15 answers; each answer is marked v15 in section 5 ('Attempt bounds of the transaction owners') and in the peel's admission. In short: the body's error chain (the attempt closure records it; the pure-Go wrapper adopts the Apple binding's retryable rule as a second client prerequisite; SimFDB's pin mutation recorded at /var/tmp/fdb-upgrade-recovery/simfdb-pin-mut/); the loop's predicate is the runner's any-cause rule (isRetriableAnyCause, errors.Join trees), the first-cause rule kept for AutoContinuingCursor; the self-committing body refused before tx.Commit with RecordContextNotActiveError, and the raw rc.Transaction().Commit() path named with its census; the exhaustion reconcile checked against the before/after model with SimFDB ground truth and a red fixture; pages write and run through Run, page-1 FaultConflict fixture; the throttled iterator's Go-only terminal classes; uncounted split-window retries take the delay; the simulated delay draws but does not move the SimClock; the route's interface (AttemptTransactor/AttemptCall); the chaos replay cases moved to FaultCommitUnknown by census; the resolver and CLI dump that call a backend directly; the catalog bootstrap's step 3 check-then-create; the setup-DDL retry tied to the target's conflict footprint; Go's peel performance criterion (whole peel <= 2.5 s at W=B and every fixture, n>=2, load recorded, a miss fixed in Go, B never raised) and the owned 1007 priced; the timing extraction over every log carrying a timing line, bound by hash (ws-d-oracle/corner-refit-rates.py/.txt, README item 32); stale references restated at tree 512ae24895a17ec693b76bfb6d6d31cd63a8ee32 (the gate tree adds only comments and documents to it). Non-design changes: comment-only corrections at pkg/recordlayer/spfresh_write.go (the split window), conformance/guardiann_probe_conformance_test.go (B's derivation), pkg/simfdb/simfdb.go (declinedRetryError's parity citation